# One guest throws into the pile and a second guest's heroine runs through the bodies it owns by
# interaction: she may not take them, and the host's world moves them at her pace through her
# copy there. Driven kinematic in flight on her world they would fling her (README "The second
# layer", Flight).
scenario authority_three_cross
scene pile60_four
seed 71
guests 3
# A hard end well past rest, so the rest measures watch the world at rest for seconds.
end 16s
light_mass 20kg
authority interaction

net g1 rtt 100ms jitter 20ms loss 2%
net g2 rtt 100ms jitter 20ms loss 2%
net g3 rtt 100ms jitter 20ms loss 2%

p1 grab ball_s as a1
p3 walk -1.2 0 as start
at 1200ms p1 throw 2 0.3 -0.1 speed 8 as t1
at 1300ms p3 walk 5.5 0 speed 4 as run
# Derived: the run starts at 1.3 s and covers 6.7 m at 4 m/s (1.68 s); the pile's 1 m at half
# speed adds 0.25 s, reaching speed and stopping within 0.2 m a quarter second: 3.5 s. A runner
# the pile holds or flings is cut off here and the run fails.
at 3500ms p3 wait 100ms as stop

expect result a1 granted
expect result run done
expect agree_at_rest 1cm 2deg
expect no_stuck
# Once at rest after the last action, a guest's world stays at rest: 0.
expect rest_breaks.count <= 0
# No pass-through: a light copy a guest's own character walks into without contact is a miss.
expect response_misses.count <= 0
# Derived: a body a guest simulates is moved by the seam only at a take, which keeps its pose
# (README "Authority follows interaction"): float noise, 1 cm.
expect local_correction.max <= 1cm
# Derived: the same correction of its turn. The stand reads an angle through acosf of a float
# dot product, 2 sqrt(2 n 2^-24) rad for a dot n ulps off 1: 0.04 deg a ulp, 0.16 deg at 16,
# which three float products of unit turns stay within; the least turn a placement shows is a
# hundredth of a radian, 0.57 deg: 0.25 deg.
expect local_turn.max <= 0.25deg
# Derived: a render offset's release, 0.15 of at most 2 m.
expect jump.max <= 0.3m
# Derived for every copy, predicted or not, against its owner's drawn picture at the copy's
# playback tick: the snap keeps its physics within 1 m of the owner's physics there, its render
# offset adds at most 2 m, and the owner's picture carries its own offset of at most 2 m (a
# placement of the owner's own, as a grab's take-over, glides there too): 5 m. A prediction in
# its pause leaves the gap (prediction_gap and flight_pause_gap, reported only).
expect aligned_gap.max <= 5m
# A cap, not a derivation: the glide's reach (SYNC_OFFSET_LOST_M, 5 m), past which the offset
# clears and the loser's picture jumps. The check is that no lost take is seen to jump; how far
# two pictures of one contested body part is chaos no bound derives.
expect lost_takes.max <= 5m
# Liveness: each rule ran at all (takes, a take of another guest's body refused, a take-back).
expect takes.count >= 1
expect take_refusals.count >= 1
expect reclaims.count >= 1
# Derived: between two take-backs a prediction's pull is paused at most (120 + 60) / 2 of any
# 120 ticks (sync_soft.h: the chain cap 60, drained a tick per tick without a touch): 90.
expect pause_window.max <= 90t
